   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Aid</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Alliance for Learning in Systems for Equitable Child and Adolescent Health (Asia Pacific)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment will contribute to better health outcomes for children and adolescents in the Pacific and Southeast Asia through strengthening systems for equitable child and adolescent health by:
1.	Increasing the availability and use of data to strengthen preventative action.
2.	Increasing the use of data and evidence-based strategies for learning, implementation and quality improvement to strengthen health systems. 
3.	Increasing the involvement of young people and communities to build trust and address power.

MCRI will achieve these aims through activities targeting immunisation, neglected tropical diseases, non-communicable diseases and health systems strengthening in Cambodia, Fiji, Indonesia, Kiribati, Laos, Papua New Guinea, the Philippines, Solomon Islands, Thailand, Tonga, Tuvalu and Vietnam.</narrative>
  </description>
